 "text": "GTA VI drops tomorrow. Millions will buy the game, but some people own the company that makes it. Wait, who owns GTA? Take-Two, Rockstar's parent company. Put one thousand dollars into Take-Two the day GTA V came out in twenty thirteen, and you'd have about thirteen thousand today. That's far more than the S&P five hundred did over the same years. And GTA V helped Take-Two nearly double its revenue in one year. But here's what most people miss. The stock had already run from about eleven dollars to eighteen before GTA V launched. Today, it jumped about seven percent, so some of the hype may already be priced in. Bank of America's price target is three hundred and thirty dollars, while the lowest analyst target is one seventy. So tomorrow, are you buying the game, the stock, or both?",
